**1. Analysis of Recent Freight Scheduling Failures**  
- **Discussion Points:**  
  - Mark Thompson reported a concerning drop in freight scheduling performance metrics for Q1 2023, with an on-time delivery rate of only 85%, a significant decline from Q4 2022 which was previously reported at 89%.  
  - Lisa Patel raised alarms about the anticipated peak season, highlighting that freight volume has unexpectedly decreased by 10% compared to the same period last year, contradicting earlier forecasts.  
  - Michael Lee noted that system upgrades have been problematic, leading to a regression in scheduling algorithms rather than the intended improvements. He expressed doubts about the effectiveness of further integration with the Transportation Management System (TMS), suggesting it could exacerbate existing route planning issues.  

- **Action Items:**  
  - Mark to conduct a comprehensive investigation into the causes of the scheduling failures and present findings by March 29, 2023.  
  - Lisa to convene an emergency meeting with stakeholders to address the declining freight volumes and strategize on potential market interventions.  
